{:proof/problem-id "apm-t01A01", :proof/classification :partial, :proof/output "\n\n---\n\nTARGET SANITY CHECK — mentions-problem-objects? ✅ (the plan and alignment explicitly reference the non-surjective map \\(f : \\mathbb{RP}^2 \\to \\mathbb{RP}^2\\), fundamental groups, and the null-homotopy). avoids-assuming-conclusion? ✅ (the Lean target assumes only non-surjectivity and derives trivial \\(f_*\\) plus null-homotopy). meaningful-without-prose? ✅ (even without Stage 1 prose, the EDN data specify the goal, required terms, and helper lemma). Notes: the helper lemma encodes the hinted retract \\( \\mathbb{RP}^2 \\setminus\\{pt\\} \\simeq S^1\\), which is essential for both conclusions.\n\n```\nPROOF-PLAN.EDN\n{:goal \"Given a non-surjective map f : RP^2 -> RP^2, prove that f_* on pi_1 is trivial and that f is null-homotopic.\"\n :terms [{:name \"Punctured RP^2\"\n          :meaning \"Removing one point leaves a Mobius band that deformation retracts onto S^1.\"\n          :needed-because \"Once f misses a point, we can replace the codomain by S^1 where pi_1 is easy.\"}\n         {:name \"Homomorphisms Z/2 -> Z\"\n          :meaning \"The only group map from pi_1(RP^2)=Z/2 to pi_1(S^1)=Z is trivial.\"\n          :needed-because \"Forces f_* to kill all loops when the image lands in the retract.\"}\n         {:name \"S^1 as K(Z,1)\"\n          :meaning \"Maps RP^2 -> S^1 are classified by induced maps on pi_1.\"\n          :needed-because \"A trivial pi_1 map implies the entire map is homotopic to a constant; composing with the inclusion back into RP^2 keeps it constant.\"}]\n :strategy [{:id :s1\n             :formal-dependency \"RP2_non_surjective_trivial_pi1\"\n             :informal-dependency \"Pick y outside the image, retract RP^2 \\\\ {y} onto S^1, show f_* factors through Z/2 -> Z -> Z/2 as zero, and use K(Z,1) classification for the null-homotopy.\"\n             :why-this-now \"This single pipeline addresses both claims simultaneously.\"\n             :lean